Feature: Aggregation of Sales Data by Brand, Product, Market, Competitor Flag, Channel, and Transaction Time

  This feature calculates the total integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars for each unique combination of brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, and transaction_timestamp from the purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly table, applying specific business rules and validation criteria.

  Background:
    Given the source table is purgo_playground.bai_sales_agg_obu_customer_datapack_weekly
    And the columns used for grouping are brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, transaction_timestamp
    And the aggregation columns are integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, integrated_dollars
    And the filter markets are "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", "rituximab market"
    And the transaction date must be within the last 36 months from cdl_effective_date
    And if brand_normalized_name is "kanjinti", "mvasi", or "riabni" and br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER", then set integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars to zero before aggregation
    And NULL values in integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars are treated as zero in aggregation

  Scenario Outline: Successful aggregation for valid rows
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And normalized_name "<product>"
    And market_normalized_name "<market>"
    And competitor_flag <competitor_flag>
    And channel_name "<channel>"
    And transaction_timestamp "<transaction_timestamp>"
    And br_gpo_flag "<br_gpo_flag>"
    And cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    And integrated_units <integrated_units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <integrated_normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <integrated_dollars>
    When the market_normalized_name is in the allowed list
    And the transaction_timestamp is within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date (transaction_timestamp >= date_add(cdl_effective_date, -36*30))
    And the brand_normalized_name is not "kanjinti", "mvasi", or "riabni" or br_gpo_flag does not contain "KAISER"
    Then the row is included in the aggregation
    And the aggregated values for the group are the sum of integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars (treating NULL as zero)

    Examples:
      | brand      | product     | market              | competitor_flag | channel      | transaction_timestamp | br_gpo_flag | cdl_effective_date | integrated_units | integrated_normalized_units | integrated_dollars |
      | kanjinti   | Herceptin   | trastuzumab-anns    | true           | Hospital     | 2023-05-01 00:00:00  | ABC         | 2023-06-01         | 100              | 90                        | 10000.00           |
      | mvasi      | Avastin     | bevacizumab-awwb    | false          | Retail       | 2022-01-15 00:00:00  | DEF         | 2022-02-01         | 200              | 180                       | 20000.00           |
      | riabni     | Rituxan     | rituximab market    | true           | Specialty    | 2021-12-01 00:00:00  | GHI         | 2022-01-01         | 150              | 140                       | 15000.00           |
      | herceptin  | Herceptin   | trastuzumab-anns    | false          | Hospital     | 2023-04-01 00:00:00  | JKL         | 2023-05-01         | 120              | 110                       | 12000.00           |

  Scenario Outline: Zeroing sales values for KAISER GPO flag and specified brands
    Given a row with brand_normalized_name "<brand>"
    And normalized_name "<product>"
    And market_normalized_name "<market>"
    And competitor_flag <competitor_flag>
    And channel_name "<channel>"
    And transaction_timestamp "<transaction_timestamp>"
    And br_gpo_flag "<br_gpo_flag>"
    And cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    And integrated_units <integrated_units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <integrated_normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <integrated_dollars>
    When the market_normalized_name is in the allowed list
    And the transaction_timestamp is within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date
    And the brand_normalized_name is "kanjinti", "mvasi", or "riabni" and br_gpo_flag contains "KAISER"
    Then the row is included in the aggregation
    And the aggregated values for the group are zero for integrated_units, integrated_normalized_units, and integrated_dollars

    Examples:
      | brand      | product     | market              | competitor_flag | channel      | transaction_timestamp | br_gpo_flag         | cdl_effective_date | integrated_units | integrated_normalized_units | integrated_dollars |
      | kanjinti   | Herceptin   | trastuzumab-anns    | true           | Hospital     | 2023-05-01 00:00:00  | KAISER PERMANENTE   | 2023-06-01         | 100              | 90                        | 10000.00           |
      | mvasi      | Avastin     | bevacizumab-awwb    | false          | Retail       | 2022-01-15 00:00:00  | KAISER              | 2022-02-01         | 200              | 180                       | 20000.00           |
      | riabni     | Rituxan     | rituximab market    | true           | Specialty    | 2021-12-01 00:00:00  | KAISER GPO          | 2022-01-01         | 150              | 140                       | 15000.00           |

  Scenario Outline: Exclusion of rows with invalid market
    Given a row with market_normalized_name "<market>"
    When the market_normalized_name is not "trastuzumab-anns", "bevacizumab-awwb", or "rituximab market"
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation

    Examples:
      | market            |
      | adalimumab-anns   |
      | infliximab market |
      | other-market      |

  Scenario Outline: Exclusion of rows with transaction date outside 36 months window
    Given a row with transaction_timestamp "<transaction_timestamp>"
    And cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When transaction_timestamp is not within 36 months prior to cdl_effective_date (transaction_timestamp < date_add(cdl_effective_date, -36*30))
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation

    Examples:
      | transaction_timestamp | cdl_effective_date |
      | 2019-01-01 00:00:00  | 2023-06-01         |
      | 2018-05-15 00:00:00  | 2022-05-01         |
      | 2017-12-31 00:00:00  | 2021-12-01         |

  Scenario Outline: Handling NULL values in sales columns
    Given a row with integrated_units <integrated_units>
    And integrated_normalized_units <integrated_normalized_units>
    And integrated_dollars <integrated_dollars>
    When any of the sales columns are NULL
    Then treat NULL as zero in aggregation

    Examples:
      | integrated_units | integrated_normalized_units | integrated_dollars |
      | NULL             | 100                        | 10000.00           |
      | 200              | NULL                       | 20000.00           |
      | 150              | 140                        | NULL               |
      | NULL             | NULL                       | NULL               |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario for invalid cdl_effective_date format
    Given a row with cdl_effective_date "<cdl_effective_date>"
    When cdl_effective_date is not a valid DATE format (e.g., not YYYY-MM-DD)
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation
    And an error message "Invalid cdl_effective_date format" is logged

    Examples:
      | cdl_effective_date |
      | 20230601           |
      | 06/01/2023         |
      | June 1, 2023       |
      | NULL               |

  Scenario Outline: Error scenario for missing required fields
    Given a row with missing required field "<missing_field>"
    When any of brand_normalized_name, normalized_name, market_normalized_name, competitor_flag, channel_name, transaction_timestamp, or cdl_effective_date is NULL
    Then the row is excluded from aggregation
    And an error message "Missing required field: <missing_field>" is logged

    Examples:
      | missing_field           |
      | brand_normalized_name   |
      | normalized_name         |
      | market_normalized_name  |
      | competitor_flag         |
      | channel_name            |
      | transaction_timestamp   |
      | cdl_effective_date      |
